<phylogeny rooted="true" rerootable="true">
  <name>Check internal taxa (demo)</name>
  <description>Synthetic mammal tree whose six tips carry their NCBI lineage as metadata fields (ncbi:class ... ncbi:species), so Analysis &gt; Check Internal Taxa against Tips &amp; NCBI runs OFFLINE, and whose four internal annotations are wrong in three different ways: &apos;genus Felidae&apos; over the cats has the wrong RANK (the tips&apos; lineages say family); &apos;order Rodentia&apos; over the cats and the dog is the wrong TAXON (no tip below it is a rodent; Carnivora is proposed); &apos;family Muridae&apos; over the mice and the human is NOT SHARED by all tips below it (Mammalia is proposed); &apos;family Muridae&apos; over the two mice is consistent. The report lists the four findings with three corrections; Apply writes them (undoable).</description>
